flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a scan on the phone reaches Paperless
    accDescr: On the phone, the scanner of the Nextcloud app saves the pages as a PDF into the folder Inbox, or the auto upload of the app takes a file from a folder of the phone into it. With the next run of Paperless Sync, at the interval that the administrator set, 5 minutes by default, the file goes to Paperless, which reads its text and makes it a document. When Paperless imports it, the file leaves the inbox; once the document has left the inbox of Paperless too, when someone finished it there, the next run writes the copy of the new document into the archive, in the folders of its correspondent, its type and its year, with the marker of its ID, such as [P123], in its name; the phone finds it there. When the import fails, such as for a damaged PDF, the file moves to the folder Failed imports, next to a .error.txt that gives the reason; a file that Paperless refuses at once, such as one of a type that it doesn't take, stays in the inbox until it changes. Your steps are orange, Nextcloud blue, Paperless-ngx green and a failed import red.

    scan["📱 Scan document in the<br>Nextcloud app: the pages<br>as one PDF"]
    auto["📱 Auto upload of a<br>folder of the phone"]
    inbox["📂 The file in the folder<br>Inbox in Nextcloud"]
    paperless{"Paperless reads<br>its text: a new<br>document?"}
    failed["Failed imports: the<br>file, next to a .error.txt<br>that gives the reason"]
    refused["Stays in Inbox<br>until it changes"]
    waiting["Waits in the inbox of<br>Paperless until someone<br>finishes the document"]
    archive["📄 The copy in Archive:<br>correspondent, type and<br>year, … [P123].pdf, also<br>on the phone"]

    scan -- "save into<br>Inbox" --> inbox
    auto -- "upload into<br>Inbox" --> inbox
    inbox -- "next run, 5 minutes<br>by default" --> paperless
    paperless -- "yes: the file<br>leaves Inbox" --> waiting
    waiting -- "next run after<br>it is finished" --> archive
    paperless -- "the import<br>fails" --> failed
    paperless -- "refused, such<br>as its type" --> refused

    classDef yours fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef refused fill:#c9302c1f,stroke:#c9302c,stroke-width:2px
    class scan,auto yours
    class inbox,archive nextcloud
    class paperless,waiting paperless
    class failed,refused refused
